{"availability":"available","full":"sethbergman/tumbletown-playground","name":"tumbletown-playground","description":"Pre-launch marketing site for a (fictional) indoor playground: plain HTML/CSS, Netlify Forms, hosted-checkout payments, self-enforcing launch gates.","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-21T19:31:41Z","updated":"2026-09-21T19:37:28Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tumbletown-playground.netlify.app","topics":["accessibility","bash","css","html","netlify","portfolio","static-site"],"demo":"https://tumbletown-playground.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:33.729Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:33.729Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:33.729Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:11:33.729Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A pre-launch marketing site for a family-owned indoor playground (ages 1 to 12). It has ten pages, three working forms, hosted-checkout payments, and a launch process that guards itself. It uses no framework and no dependencies, and it has no build toolchain to rot.","About this repository. I built this for a real small-business client. The client went with an all-in-one venue platform instead, so I have published the work with every identifying detail replaced. Tumbletown, Maya Lindqvist and the family story are fictional, the logo is a stand-in, and example.com stands in for the domain. The code, structure, commit history and engineering decisions are all unchanged.","This site will outlive whoever maintains it next. A brochure site with a toolchain is a site that stops building in two years when a transitive dependency breaks, and the person holding it is a playground owner, not a developer. Nothing here needs npm, and nothing here can rot."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sethbergman/tumbletown-playground/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9192e9a